SO-101 to PiPER Local Teleoperation

This distribution extracts the locally developed SO-101/PiPER bridge from an
XLeRobot/LeRobot development checkout. New portable packaging and documentation
are provided under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The upstream checkout's Apache-2.0 license and original Hugging Face copyright
notice are preserved in LICENSE. LeRobot itself is an optional dependency,
not vendored here. LeRobot is copyright the Hugging Face team and contributors,
licensed under Apache-2.0: https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot

The CAN wire format was implemented with reference to AgileX's piper_sdk
(protocol v2, source revision c9e8a281) and Agilex-College examples:
https://github.com/agilexrobotics/piper_sdk
https://github.com/agilexrobotics/Agilex-College

SocketCAN error decoding references Linux v6.8 gs_usb.c / can/error.h and
candleLight firmware v2.0 src/can.c. Those projects retain their own licenses;
no Linux or candleLight C source is bundled in this distribution.
https://github.com/torvalds/linux
https://github.com/candle-usb/candleLight_fw

PiPER and AgileX are names of their respective owners. This project is an
independent integration and is not an official manufacturer release.
